  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Draft Sec.3, amends TCA 2-7-112(c)(1) (removed by HA0138; not in Chaptered)\n(quote) Tennessee Code Annotated, Section 2-7-112(c)(1), is amended by adding the language \"that is not a temporary driver license\" immediately after the language \"Tennessee driver license\".\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) Sec.1, new TCA 2-2-401(a) (Chaptered)\n(quote) (a) The coordinator of elections, in collaboration with the department of safety, shall, prior to January 1, 2028, create a secure, electronic portal through which each county administrator of elections may access information to verify, prior to processing an applicant's application to register to vote, whether the applicant is a United States citizen based upon records on file at the time of issuance of the most recent driver license or identification card or other credential from the department of safety.\n(section) Sec.1, new TCA 2-2-401(d) (Chaptered)\n(quote) (d) If a county administrator rejects an application based upon information received pursuant to this section, the administrator shall provide written notice to the applicant of the applicant's right to appeal the decision in accordance with\n(section) Draft Sec.5, amends TCA 55-50-321(c)(1)(C) (removed by HA0138; not in Chaptered)\n(quote) (C) Any applicant applying for a driver license, instruction permit, intermediate driver license, or photo identification license, upon initial issuance or reinstatement, shall provide either an original or certified copy of documentation that the applicant is a citizen of the United States.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Draft Sec.7, amends TCA 55-50-331(g)(3): licence marker tied to voting (removed; not in Chaptered)\n(quote) (3) A temporary driver license, temporary photo identification license, or temporary permit must include a visually distinctive font or color for the class designation on the face of the license to distinguish the temporary license from the license issued to United States citizens under § 55-50-303(a)(9) that are used as a photo identification for voting purposes.\n(section) Sec.1, new TCA 2-2-403 (Chaptered): funding condition\n(quote) It is the intent that this part be funded by federal grant funding. This part has no effect until such sufficient funding has been obtained.\n(other) Sec.1 (Chaptered): new Part 4 'Verification of Voter Eligibility'. 2-2-401: citizenship portal, built by the coordinator of elections with the department of safety before Jan 1, 2028; an agreement sets what the administrator submits, what the portal returns (no record or several records), a backup method, misuse and penalties; portal data is confidential. 2-2-402: a parallel portal with the Tennessee bureau of investigation for Tennessee felony-conviction eligibility, with loss of access for misuse. 2-2-403: part has no effect until federal grant funding is obtained. 2-2-404: severability.\n(other) Sec.2: 2-2-125(b): written notice of a right to appeal a rejection to the commission within ten days, with an appeal form.\n(other) Sec.3 (Chaptered): 38-6-118(d)(3): bureau shares expunged-record information with the coordinator of elections on request to decide eligibility to register or vote.\n(other) Draft Sec.4-8 (all removed by HA0138): 55-50-303(a)(9) licence for non-citizens narrowed to citizens; 55-50-321(c)(1)(C) citizenship documents for licences/photo IDs; 55-50-321(i)(1) proof of citizenship for people with out-of-state licences from states that license illegal aliens; 55-50-331(g) temporary licences for lawful permanent residents and authorised stay (up to 8 years), distinct font/colour, LPR renewals on or after Jan 1, 2026 need citizenship proof; 55-50-102(56) definition change.\n(other) Draft Sec.11: Sec.1, 2, 9 effective on becoming law; remaining sections effective Jan 1, 2026 (rules and licence redesign earlier). Chaptered Sec.6: effective on becoming law (signed 2025-05-21).\n(other) version: Draft 3041021 (Lamberth): carries slot a (Sec.3 temporary-licence exclusion from 2-7-112(c)(1)), slot d (Sec.1 portal that checks whether the applicant is a NON-citizen; Sec.5 citizenship documents for licence issuance) and slot e (Sec.7 licence marker).\n(other) version: Draft 3054708: same operative text as 3041021; only the header adds the SB 133 companion line.\n(other) version: HA0138 (House State and Local Government amendment 1, full rewrite): drops Draft Sections 3-8 and 11; keeps the two portals, the appeal notice and adds 38-6-118(d)(3) and the bureau-misuse rule; the citizenship portal text still reads 'a non-United States citizen based upon records on file'; no slot a text. Skeleton flags adopted=0; the action log says adopted 2025-04-21.\n(other) version: HA0139 (amendment 2): replaces 2-2-401 with the agreement/confidentiality version (verifies 'a United States citizen based upon records on file at the time of issuance of the most recent driver license or identification card or other credential') and adds the 2-2-403 federal-grant funding clause; adopted 2025-04-21 per the action log.\n(other) version: Chaptered 3245912 (Pub. Ch. 473): equals HA0138 + HA0139; no licence-citizenship or temporary-licence text; no slot a or c text.\n(other) note: Enacted law puts no duty on applicants to show proof: county administrators check applicants' citizenship through a department-of-safety portal built before 2028 and funded only if federal grants are obtained. Companion SB 133. Amendment adoption flags in the data are all 0; adoption of HA0138 and HA0139 comes from the action log lines on 2025-04-21 and from the Chaptered text, which matches them. HA0138 and HA0139 are headed 'House State and Local Government' (committee amendments); the log shows their formal adoption on the floor, so which committee votes were on the amended text is not certain.",
